codex
Step 0 now rules out the existing workaround as well: its “reference” scan tries 9,998 moduli, but the tags were deliberately generated so their within-block differences have gcd exactly \(q\). Euclid’s algorithm recovers \(q\) directly, so the alleged two-million-operation mechanical route and the 154-operation compact route are the same route in disguise. I’m measuring that stronger attack and the originally proposed dense planted-cycle baseline before deciding whether a paper-grounded alternative survives.
codex
The local deliverable is now complete and the repository’s own submission preflight confirms all nine gates pass, G8 is present, and all six attacks have zero successes. Preflight stops exactly where it should: the bare transcript contains only account-limit errors from two vendors, so it cannot support a hardness verdict. I’m doing the final file/schema audit now; no `REJECTED.md` will be written because the family itself did not fail.
All local implementation and reporting work is complete. The harness and both G9 arms were executed but could not obtain scored calls because the supplied OpenRouter account returned an account-wide 403 total-limit error.
